<div>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="mb-12">
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm mb-4">
            <a href="/docs/builtins" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Built-ins</a>
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-gray-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-white">Testing</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl mb-6">
            <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-lime-400 to-green-400 bg-clip-text text-transparent">Testing Functions</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-8">
            Test DSL with describe/it blocks, assertions, and factory functions.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Test DSL -->
    <section id="section-test-dsl" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-lime-500/20 flex items-center justify-center">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-lime-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m-6 9l2 2 4-4" />
                </svg>
            </span>
            Test DSL
        </h2>

        <section id="def-describe" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-describe" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">describe(description, def)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Define a test group. <code class="text-amber-400">context</code> is an alias.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="def-test" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-test" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">test(description, def)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Define an individual test case.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="def-it" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-it" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">it(description, def)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Alternative to test(). <code class="text-amber-400">specify</code> is an alias.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Example</h3>
            <pre data-filename="test_example.sl"><code class="language-soli text-sm">describe("Calculator", fn() {
  test("adds numbers", fn() {
    assert_eq(add(1, 2), 3)
  })

  it("subtracts numbers", fn() {
    assert_eq(subtract(5, 3), 2)
  })

  describe("division", fn() {
    it("divides numbers", fn() {
      assert_eq(divide(10, 2), 5)
    })

    it("handles division by zero", fn() {
      assert_raises("division by zero", fn() { divide(1, 0) })
    })
  })
})</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Declarations are read, not run</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">The runner reads the spec tree from the file without running the <code class="text-amber-400">describe</code> bodies. Anything it cannot register fails the file with <code>N spec declaration problem(s)</code>, one line each &mdash; instead of being silently dropped:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 text-sm space-y-1">
                <li>a <code>describe</code>/<code>context</code>/<code>test</code>/<code>it</code>/<code>specify</code> inside a top-level <code>if</code>, <code>unless</code>, loop or <code>try</code>;</li>
                <li>a <code>test</code> outside any <code>describe</code>;</li>
                <li>any other statement in a <code>describe</code> body (<code>url = "/posts"</code>, a <code>def</code>&hellip;) &mdash; only tests, nested suites, hooks and <code>viewport</code> belong there;</li>
                <li>a suite or test name that is not a string literal (interpolated or computed);</li>
                <li>a second <code>before_each</code> (or any other hook) in the same <code>describe</code>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">Shared variables and helper functions go at the top level of the file; reassign them in a <code>before_each</code>. To skip a suite when a service is missing, call <a href="#def-requires-solidb" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline"><code>requires_solidb()</code></a> or <code>skip("why")</code> in its <code>before_each</code>.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup & Teardown -->
    <section id="section-hooks" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Setup & Teardown</h2>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-before-each" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-before-each" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">before_each(def)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Run before each test</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-after-each" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-after-each" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">after_each(def)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Run after each test</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-before-all" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-before-all" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">before_all(def)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Run once before all tests</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-after-all" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-after-all" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">after_all(def)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Run once after all tests</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-pending" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-pending" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">pending(reason?)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Mark test as pending (not yet implemented) and stop its body. Not a failure: the file passes and the summary counts it apart (<code>12 tests, 2 pending</code>).</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-skip" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-skip" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">skip(reason?)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Stop the current test and count it as pending, like <code>pending()</code>. Called in a <code>before_each</code>, it skips every test of the suite.</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Nesting and failures</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 text-sm space-y-1 mb-4">
                <li>Nested suites inherit hooks: every enclosing <code>before_each</code> runs, outermost first; <code>after_each</code> hooks run innermost first.</li>
                <li>A raising <code>before_each</code> fails the test with <code>before_each: &lt;error&gt;</code> and its body does not run. A raising <code>after_each</code> fails the test (<code>after_each: &hellip;</code>). Teardown hooks always run.</li>
                <li>A raising <code>before_all</code> fails the suite &mdash; <code>&lt;suite&gt; (before_all, N test(s) not run)</code> &mdash; without running its tests; a raising <code>after_all</code> is reported as a failure.</li>
                <li>One hook of each kind per <code>describe</code>. Write the block with parentheses: <code>before_each() do &hellip; end</code> &mdash; a bare <code>before_each do</code> does not parse.</li>
            </ul>
            <pre data-filename="cart_spec.sl"><code class="language-soli text-sm">cart = []                      # shared state lives at the top level

describe("Cart") do
  before_each() do
    cart = ["book"]
  end

  describe("with a gift") do
    before_each() do           # runs after the outer one
      cart.push("wrapping")
    end

    test("holds both items") do
      assert_eq(cart, ["book", "wrapping"])
    end
  end

  test("starts with the book only") do
    assert_eq(cart, ["book"])
  end
end</code></pre>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Assertions -->
    <section id="section-assertions" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Assertions</h2>

        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">
            Assertions are builtins of the test runner &mdash; available inside any <code class="text-cyan-400">test(...)</code> body, with nothing to import. Each <strong class="text-white">raises</strong> on failure (the runner prints the values, the file and the line) and returns <code>1</code> on success, bumping the run's assertion counter. Every <code class="text-cyan-400">assert_*</code> takes an <strong class="text-white">optional trailing message</strong>, prefixed to the failure. <code class="text-cyan-400">assert</code> and <code class="text-cyan-400">assert_not</code> require a real boolean &mdash; use <code class="text-cyan-400">assert_not_null</code> for presence. Full reference: <a href="/docs/testing#def-assert" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">Testing &rarr; Assertions</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">On failure</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">An assertion raises; the runner catches it, marks the test failed, and prints a message that shows the values, with the file and line. A custom check is just a function that <code class="text-cyan-400">throw</code>s.</p>
            <pre data-filename="Failure messages"><code class="language-soli text-sm">assert_eq(cart.length, 3)                  # expected 3, got 2
assert_eq(cart.length, 3, "the cart size") # the cart size: expected 3, got 2
assert_null(post.deleted_at)               # expected nil, got "2026-01-01"
assert_gt(total, 0)                        # expected -5 to be greater than 0
assert_match(slug, "^[a-z-]+$")            # expected "Hello" to match /^[a-z-]+$/
assert("yes")                              # assert expects a Bool, got string ("yes")</code></pre>
            <pre data-filename="Custom assertion"><code class="language-soli text-sm">def assert_length(collection, expected)
  actual = collection.length
  throw "expected #{expected} items, got #{actual}" unless actual == expected
end</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Basic Assertions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-assert" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert(condition)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert condition is <code>true</code> (a Bool; anything else fails and names its type)</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-not" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-not" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_not(condition)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert condition is false</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-eq" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-eq" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_eq(a, b)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert a equals b</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-ne" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-ne" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_ne(a, b)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert a does not equal b</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Null & Comparison</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-assert-null" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-null" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_null(value)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert value is null</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-not-null" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-not-null" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_not_null(value)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert value is not null</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-gt" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-gt" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_gt(a, b)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert a > b</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-lt" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-lt" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_lt(a, b)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert a < b</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Advanced Assertions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-assert-match" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-match" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_match(str, pattern)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert string matches regex</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-contains" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-contains" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_contains(coll, val)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert collection contains value</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-hash-has-key" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-hash-has-key" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_hash_has_key(h, k)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert hash has key</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-json" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-json" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_json(string)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Assert string is valid JSON</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <section id="def-assert-raises" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-assert-raises" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">assert_raises(fragment?) do ... end</code>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Passes when the block raises &mdash; and, given a fragment, when the error message contains it &mdash; and <strong class="text-white">returns the error message</strong> so you can assert more on it. Fails when the block raises nothing or a different error. A failed assertion or a <code>skip</code>/<code>pending</code> inside the block is not taken for the expected error: it propagates. Also takes a lambda: <code>assert_raises(fn() { ... })</code>. Keep the parentheses &mdash; <code>assert_raises do</code> does not parse.</p>
                <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">message = assert_raises("out of stock") do
  cart.add(sold_out_item)
end
assert_contains(message, sold_out_item.sku)

assert_raises() do
  Invoice.new({}).finalize!
end</code></pre>
            </div>
        </section>
    </section>

    <!-- Expect API -->
    <section id="section-expect" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Expect API</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">Chainable assertion API for expressive testing. Use <code class="text-amber-400">expect(value)</code> followed by chainable methods.</p>

        <section id="def-expect" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-expect" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Creates an expectation with the given value. Chain with <code class="text-amber-400">to_*()</code> methods.</p>
                <div class="mt-4">
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">expect(42).to_equal(42);
expect("hello").to_contain("ell");
expect(10).to_be_greater_than(5);
expect(user).to_not_be_null();</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Equality Assertions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-expect-to-be" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_be(expected)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value is same as expected (identity)</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-equal" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-equal" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_equal(expected)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value equals expected (value equality)</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-not-be" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-not-be" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_not_be(expected)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value is not the same as expected</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-not-equal" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-not-equal" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_not_equal(expected)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value does not equal expected</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Null Assertions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-expect-to-be-null" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be-null" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_be_null()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value is null</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-not-be-null" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-not-be-null" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_not_be_null()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value is not null</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Comparison Assertions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-expect-to-be-gt" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be-gt" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_be_greater_than(n)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value > n</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-be-lt" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be-lt" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_be_less_than(n)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value < n</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-be-gte" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be-gte" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_be_greater_than_or_equal(n)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value >= n</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-be-lte" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be-lte" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_be_less_than_or_equal(n)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts value <= n</p>
                </section>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">The comparisons (and <code>assert_gt</code>/<code>assert_lt</code>) accept an Int and a Float mixed: <code>expect(3).to_be_greater_than(2.5)</code>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Collection/String Assertions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-expect-to-contain" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-contain" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(value).to_contain(item)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts array or string contains item</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-match" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-match" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(string).to_match(text)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts string <strong class="text-white">contains</strong> <code>text</code> &mdash; a substring check, not a regex (use <code>assert_match</code> for a pattern)</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-have-key" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-have-key" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(hash).to_have_key(key)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts hash has the key</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-expect-to-be-valid-json" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-expect-to-be-valid-json" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">expect(string).to_be_valid_json()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts string is valid JSON</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Test helpers -->
    <section id="section-test-helpers" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Test Helpers</h2>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <section id="def-with-transaction" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">with_transaction(block)</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Begin → run block → always rollback (never commits). Reads inside the block do not see its writes</p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-freeze-time" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">freeze_time(ts)</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Pin <code>datetime_now()</code>; cleared before each test</p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-travel-to" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">travel_to(ts)</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Alias for <code>freeze_time</code></p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-unfreeze-time" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">unfreeze_time()</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Restore wall-clock time</p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-requires-solidb" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">requires_solidb()</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Call in a <code>before_each</code>: skips the test (<code>needs SoliDB: &hellip;</code>) when the models' <code>SOLIDB_HOST</code> fails its health check. Under <code>SOLI_REQUIRE_DB=1</code> the skip becomes a failure</p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-requires-solikv" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">requires_solikv()</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Same for SoliKV: a <code>PING</code> to <code>SOLIKV_RESP_HOST</code>/<code>SOLIKV_RESP_PORT</code></p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-solidb-available" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">solidb_available?()</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">The same probe, as a Bool</p>
            </section>
            <section id="def-solikv-available" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">solikv_available?()</code>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">The same probe for SoliKV, as a Bool</p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Factory Functions -->
    <section id="section-factories" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Factory Functions</h2>

        <section id="def-factory-define" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-factory-define" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.define(name, data)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Define a factory with a static hash or callable block. <code>#{n}</code> in a string becomes a per-factory counter on each <code>create</code> &mdash; write it in a <strong class="text-white">raw string</strong> (<code>r"user#{n}@test.com"</code>): in a normal string Soli interpolates <code>#{n}</code> first and fails with <code>Undefined variable 'n'</code>.</p>
                <div class="mt-4">
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">Factory.define("user", {
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": r"user#{n}@test.com"
})

Factory.define("post", fn() {
  {"title": "Post #{Factory.sequence("post")}"}
})</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="def-factory-create" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-factory-create" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.create(name)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Create an instance from a factory.</p>
                <div class="mt-4">
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">user = Factory.create("user")
println(user["name"])  # "Test User"</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="def-factory-create-with" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-6">
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                <a href="#def-factory-create-with" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                    <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.create_with(name, overrides)</code>
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                    </svg>
                </a>
                <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Create an instance with custom overrides.</p>
                <div class="mt-4">
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">admin = Factory.create_with("user", { "role": "admin" })
println(admin["role"])  # "admin"
println(admin["name"])  # "Test User" (from factory)</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-factory-create-list" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-factory-create-list" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.create_list(name, count)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Create multiple instances</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-factory-sequence" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-factory-sequence" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.sequence(name)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Get auto-incrementing number</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-factory-bind" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-factory-bind" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.bind(name, Model)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Associate factory with a model class</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-factory-insert" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-factory-insert" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.insert(name, overrides?)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Build + <code>Model.create</code></p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-factory-clear" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-factory-clear" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">Factory.clear</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Clear definitions, bindings, sequences</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">View Introspection (E2E)</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">After a <code>get</code>/<code>post</code>/… request that renders a view, these helpers inspect what was rendered. They report nothing for a redirect or a JSON response. See the <a href="/docs/testing" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300">testing guide</a> for the full E2E flow.</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-assigns" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assigns" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assigns()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">All view locals as a hash (<code>{}</code> if none): the controller&rsquo;s <code>@fields</code> (not <code>_</code>-prefixed), with or without an explicit <code>render(...)</code>, plus any <code>render</code> data keys</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assign" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assign" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assign(key)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">One view local, or <code>null</code></p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-view-path" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-view-path" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">view_path()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Rendered template path, e.g. <code>"posts/index.html"</code> (<code>""</code> if none)</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-render-template" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-render-template" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">render_template()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Did the response render a view? (<code>render_template?()</code> is an alias)</p>
                </section>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-4">Very large locals (&approx;48&nbsp;KB+) degrade to a keys-only <code>assigns()</code>: keys present, values <code>null</code>.</p>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3 mt-8">Query Assertions (E2E)</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">Every response records the AQL queries the request ran (from the same log behind the dev bar's N+1 badge). Assert against it to catch a query issued in a loop, or to hold an endpoint to a query budget. See the <a href="/docs/testing" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300">testing guide</a>.</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <section id="def-assert-no-n-plus-one" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-no-n-plus-one" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_no_n_plus_one(res)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Fails if any AQL template fired 2+ times (a loop that should be batched)</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-no-ungrouped-reads" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-no-ungrouped-reads" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_no_ungrouped_reads(res)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Fails if 3+ <em>distinct</em> reads each cost a round-trip outside a <code>grouped</code> block &mdash; the case an N+1 scan cannot see, since each template ran only once</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-query-count" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-query-count" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_query_count(res, n)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts the request ran exactly <code>n</code> queries</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-max-queries" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-max-queries" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_max_queries(res, n)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Asserts the request ran at most <code>n</code> queries</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-query-count-key" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-query-count-key" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">res["query_count"] / res["n_plus_one"]</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Raw count and <code>{query, count}</code> groups behind the assertions</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-fail-on-n1" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-fail-on-n1" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">soli test --fail-on-n1</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Suite-wide guard: fails any request spec that triggers an N+1, no per-test <code>assert_no_n_plus_one</code> needed</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Browser Testing -->
    <section id="section-browser" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Browser Testing</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">Available in browser specs, run with <code class="text-cyan-400">soli test --browser</code>. Positive assertions wait for the condition; negative ones check immediately. Pass <code class="text-cyan-400">{"timeout": 30}</code> to override the 10-second default. See <a href="/docs/testing-browser" class="text-cyan-400 hover:text-cyan-300 underline">Browser Testing</a> for the full guide.</p>

        <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
            <div class="space-y-4">
                <section id="def-visit" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-visit" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">visit(path)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Navigate the browser; relative paths hit this worker's test server</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-click" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-click" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">click(selector)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Dispatch a real mouse click at the element's position</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-click-link" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-click-link" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">click_link(text)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Click a link by its visible text</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-click-button" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-click-button" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">click_button(label)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Click a button by its label or value</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-fill-in" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-fill-in" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">fill_in(field, value)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Type into a field found by selector, label, name or placeholder</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-select-option" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-select-option" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">select_option(select, option)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Choose an option by value or visible text</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-check" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-check" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">check(box) / uncheck(box)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Tick or untick a checkbox</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-choose" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-choose" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">choose(radio)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Select a radio button</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-press" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-press" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">press(key)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Press a key or chord, e.g. <code>Enter</code> or <code>Alt+d</code></p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-page-text" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-page-text" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">page_text() / page_html()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">The page's visible text, or its full markup</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-page-path" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-page-path" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">page_path() / page_url() / page_title()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Where the browser is, and what the page is called</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-evaluate" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-evaluate" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">evaluate(expression)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Run JavaScript in the page and get the value back, types preserved</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-viewport" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-viewport" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">viewport(preset) / viewport(width, height)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">The size the page renders at. Declared in a <code>describe</code> body it covers every test in the suite (nested suites inherit it); called inside a test it resizes there and then. Presets: <code>mobile</code>, <code>iphone</code>, <code>iphone_se</code>, <code>android</code>, <code>tablet</code>, <code>ipad</code>, <code>laptop</code>, <code>desktop</code>, <code>wide</code> &mdash; the device ones also emulate pixel ratio and touch. No arguments reads the current viewport back. Default 1280&times;800</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-screenshot" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-screenshot" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">screenshot(path)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Write a PNG of the current view</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-wait-for" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-wait-for" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">wait_for(selector)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Block until an element exists</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-wait-for-text" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-wait-for-text" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">wait_for_text(text)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Block until the text appears</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-text" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-text" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_text(text)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Waits for the page to show <code>text</code>; <code>assert_no_text</code> checks immediately</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-selector" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-selector" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_selector(selector)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Waits for the element; <code>assert_no_selector</code> checks immediately</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-page-path" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-page-path" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_page_path(path)</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Waits until the browser is at <code>path</code></p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-assert-no-page-errors" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-assert-no-page-errors" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">assert_no_page_errors()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Fails if the page threw or logged an error</p>
                </section>

                <section id="def-page-errors" class="scroll-mt-20">
                    <a href="#def-page-errors" class="group flex items-center gap-2">
                        <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">page_errors()</code>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">The captured JavaScript errors, as an array</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</div>
